cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below. If you cite a measured figure, cite the commit and the split it came from."
title: "Project CRADLE: One command over sword, defender, sentinel and memory — the composition, not a fifth part."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: CDDL-1.1
type: software
abstract: >-
  CRADLE orchestrates four parts that live in a sibling project: Project_FLAMING_SWORD,
  providing `tools/sword.py` (FLAMING SWORD), `tools/defender.py` (defender),
  `tools/sentinel.py` (THE REAPER) and `tools/memory_bridge.py` (THE GRIMOIRE).
  CRADLE is the composition, not a fifth part — it wires the parts together and
  reports missing siblings via `--doctor` rather than assuming they exist.
authors:
  - name: "Project CRADLE contributors"
keywords:
  - orchestration
  - composition
  - static analysis
  - code quality
  - open source
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Project FLAMING SWORD"
    notes: "Sibling project providing the four parts CRADLE orchestrates."
    url: "https://github.com/myzticalbabe/azazael/tree/main/Project_FLAMING_SWORD"